  "final_answer": "Based on an audit of the Angular frontend codebase (`ui-ngx`), modifying or deleting the backend endpoint `GET /api/converters/list` is **SAFE** and has **no impact** on the Angular frontend.\n\n### Analysis & Findings\n1. **No References Found**: There are no occurrences or references of `/api/converters/list` or `/converters/list` in any of the TypeScript, HTML, or routing files.\n2. **Current Implementation**: The Angular application retrieves list data for converters via `ConverterService` (located in `ui-ngx/src/app/core/http/converter.service.ts`), which relies exclusively on the following endpoints:\n   - **`GET /api/converters`** (using query parameters for pagination, edge templates, and integration types) via:\n     ```typescript\n     this.http.get<PageData<Converter>>(`/api/converters${pageLink.toQuery()}`, ...)\n     ```\n   - **`GET /api/converters?converterIds={ids}`** for fetching multiple specific converters.\n   - **`GET /api/converter/{converterId}`** for fetching a single converter.\n\n### Conclusion\nBecause the frontend exclusively interacts with `GET /api/converters` for paginated list retrieval, the endpoint `GET /api/converters/list` is not utilized by the user interface. Therefore, modifying or deleting it is **SAFE** (non-breaking) for the Angular frontend.",
